IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sfa-core`
IMPORT `sfa-definitions-rest`

-- Tests for sfa-definitions-rest.
-- Expected values are written from the text of the Act (the quote lines in the module under test), never from its output.

-- the context does not displace the definitions
#ASSERT `s 2(1) the definitions apply unless the context otherwise requires` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "unless the context otherwise requires": the definitions do not govern here
#ASSERT `s 2(1) the definitions apply unless the context otherwise requires` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- the context does not displace: the definition's answer stands
#ASSERT `s 2(1) the answer under a definition, allowing for the context` FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the definition's "no" stands
#ASSERT `s 2(1) the answer under a definition, allowing for the context` FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not covered stays not covered
#ASSERT `s 2(1) the answer under a definition, allowing for the context` FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- the context displaces the definition: the text gives no other meaning
#ASSERT `s 2(1) the answer under a definition, allowing for the context` TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING

-- the affairs of a corporation include: limb the matter is the promotion, formation, membership, control, business, trading, transactions, dealings, property, liabilities, profits, income, receipts, losses, outgoings or expenditure of the corporation
#ASSERT (`s 2(2) the matter is within the affairs of a corporation` WITH `a contrary intention appears in the provision` IS FALSE, `the matter is the promotion, formation, membership, control, business, trading, transactions, dealings, property, liabilities, profits, income, receipts, losses, outgoings or expenditure of the corporation` IS TRUE, `the corporation is a trustee, is not a trustee corporation, and the matter is who the beneficiaries are, their rights under the trust, or payments they have received or are entitled to` IS FALSE, `the matter is the internal management and proceeding of the corporation` IS FALSE, `the matter is an act or thing done by or on behalf of the corporation, or to or in relation to it or its business or property` IS FALSE, `at that time a receiver or a receiver and manager is in possession of, or has control over, property of the corporation` IS FALSE, `at that time the corporation is under judicial management` IS FALSE, `at that time a compromise or arrangement under section 210 of the Companies Act 1967 or section 71 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018 is being administered` IS FALSE, `at that time the corporation is being wound up` IS FALSE, `the matter is the conduct of such a receiver, receiver and manager, judicial manager, person administering such a compromise or arrangement, liquidator or provisional liquidator` IS FALSE, `the matter is the ownership of shares in, debentures of, units of shares or debentures in, or units in a collective investment scheme issued by, the corporation` IS FALSE, `the matter is the power of persons to exercise, or to control the exercise of, the votes attached to shares in the corporation, or to dispose of or control the disposal of such shares` IS FALSE, `the matter is the ascertainment of the persons who are or have been financially interested in the success or failure of the corporation, or able to control or materially influence its policy` IS FALSE, `the matter is the circumstances in which a person acquired or disposed of, or became entitled to acquire or dispose of, shares, debentures, units of shares or debentures, or units in a collective investment scheme issued by the corporation` IS FALSE, `the corporation has issued units in a collective investment scheme and the matter concerns the undertaking, scheme, common enterprise or investment contract to which they relate` IS FALSE, `the matter relates to or arises out of the audit of, or the working papers or reports of an auditor concerning, a matter in the other limbs` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
